            {
              "text": "When drafting **testamentary trusts**, **enduring powers of attorney (EPOAs)**, and **comprehensive wills**, engaging a solicitor who concentrates specifically on Queensland succession law is essential. A testamentary discretionary trust requires strict drafting to ensure tax-effectiveness, asset protection, and compliance with Queensland trust and succession legislation.\n\nThe leading law practices and succession lawyers servicing **Carindale, Wynnum, and the Brisbane East/Bayside area** include:\n\n---\n\n### **1. Carindale & Brisbane East Specialists**\n\n#### **Willwise – Judy Hayward (Carindale)**\n* **Location:** Carindale (also provides mobile/home consultations across Brisbane East & Bayside).\n* **Specialisation:** Pure succession law practice. Judy Hayward is a **Queensland Law Society (QLS) Accredited Specialist in Succession Law**—the gold standard in Queensland for complex estate planning.\n* **Key Strengths:** \n  * Will drafting and testamentary trust structures (both discretionary and capital-protected trusts).\n  * Tailored Enduring Powers of Attorney (EPOA) and Advance Health Directives (AHD).\n  * Advice on superannuation death benefit nominations (BDBNs) and family trust control.\n* **Best For:** Clients wanting an independent, highly accredited succession specialist who works on fixed-fee packages and provides personal, direct attention.\n\n#### **Fulljames Law (Carindale)**\n* **Location:** Carindale.\n* **Specialisation:** Boutique private client firm handling wills, estate planning, and deceased estate administration.\n* **Key Strengths:** Focuses on clear, accessible fixed-fee estate planning packages, ranging from basic wills to full succession plans that include business entities and enduring powers of attorney.\n* **Best For:** Families and local business owners looking for a modern, approachable local lawyer.\n\n---\n\n### **2. Wynnum & Bayside Specialists**\n\n#### **Connor Hunter Lawyers (Wynnum)**\n* **Location:** Wynnum (Bay Terrace / Tingal Rd precinct; also offices in Cleveland).\n* **Specialisation:** Established in 1971, Connor Hunter is one of the most reputable, long-standing law firms in Brisbane Bayside.\n* **Key Strengths:** \n  * Comprehensive estate planning for complex and blended family situations.\n  * Multi-generational asset protection, testamentary trusts, and executor structuring.\n  * Full-service capabilities if you need commercial, property, or conveyancing cross-advice linked to your estate assets.\n* **Best For:** Bayside families wanting an established local firm with deep historical roots and multi-disciplinary experience.\n\n#### **Queensland Legal Practice (Wynnum)**\n* **Location:** Level 5, 182 Bay Terrace, Wynnum.\n* **Specialisation:** Estate planning, deceased estates, and succession matters.\n* **Key Strengths:** Advises on tailored estate structures, proxies, testamentary trusts, and enduring powers of attorney to minimise post-death disputes and protect vulnerable beneficiaries.\n* **Best For:** Wynnum locals seeking convenient walk-in access right in the heart of Bay Terrace.\n\n#### **McCarthy Durie Lawyers (MDL) (Servicing Wynnum, Manly & Redlands)**\n* **Location:** Offices in Cleveland and Brisbane CBD (heavily servicing the broader Bayside/East suburbs).\n* **Specialisation:** One of the largest and most established legal firms in the eastern/bayside corridor (over 45 years in practice).\n* **Key Strengths:** \n  * Dedicated Wills & Estates division handling everything from straightforward wills to high-net-worth estate structuring and testamentary trusts.\n  * High competency in business succession, self-managed super funds (SMSFs), and cross-collateralised family entities.\n* **Best For:** Individuals with complex asset arrangements (companies, unit trusts, investment property portfolios) requiring high-tier institutional capacity.\n\n---\n\n### **Summary Recommendation**\n\n* **If your primary goal is a Queensland Law Society Accredited Specialist** with deep technical knowledge of testamentary trusts and asset protection, reach out to **Judy Hayward at Willwise (Carindale)**.\n* **If you prefer an established, full-service local law office in the Bayside hub**, contact **Connor Hunter Lawyers (Wynnum)**.\n* **If your estate involves commercial businesses, multiple companies, or SMSFs**, consult **McCarthy Durie Lawyers**.\n\n### **Questions to Ask During Your Initial Consultation**\n1. **Accreditation:** *Do you have a QLS Accredited Succession Law Specialist overseeing or drafting the documents?*\n2. **Fixed Pricing:** *Do you provide a fixed-fee quote for an estate planning package (e.g., standard mirror wills vs. testamentary discretionary trusts + EPOAs)?*\n3. **Non-Estate Assets:** *How will you integrate non-estate assets like family trusts, private companies, and superannuation death benefit nominations into this plan?*",
              "thoughtSignature": ""
            }
